]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in St. Mary&rsquo;s County has a record running from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025, October to November finished at 46% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 36% of normal and April to May at 50%. On grid 22414, the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 sits at 115.2, and that number can still move.</p>"}
